  "content": [
    {
      "text": "the Messiah to come 600 years after Lehi1 left Jerusalem, 1 Ne. 10:4 (19:8; 2 Ne. 25:19). Nephi1 sees virgin carried away in the Spirit, mother of the Son of God, 1 Ne. 11:13–14, 18–20. Christ to come among Jews, more wicked part of world, 2 Ne. 10:3. save Christ should come, all men must perish, 2 Ne. 11:6. virgin shall conceive and bear son, Immanuel, 2 Ne. 17:14 (Isa. 7:14). unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given, 2 Ne. 19:6 (Isa. 9:6). God shall come down from heaven among men, Mosiah 3:5 (4:2; 7:27; 13:34; 15:1; 17:8). whoso should believe that Christ should come might receive remission of sins, Mosiah 3:13. if Christ did not come, there could be no redemption, Mosiah 16:6. the Son to be born of Mary at Jerusalem, Alma 7:10. Lehi1, Nephi1, almost all fathers have testified of coming of Christ, Hel. 8:22. in five years comes the Son, Hel. 14:2. signs to be given of Christ’s coming, Hel. 14:3–6 (3 Ne. 1:15–21). on the morrow come I into world, 3 Ne. 1:13–14. I came unto my own, and my own received me not, 3 Ne. 9:16. scriptures concerning Christ’s coming are fulfilled, 3 Ne. 9:16. Christ is come not to destroy, but to fulfill, 3 Ne. 12:17 (Matt. 5:17).",
